1
00:00:00,087 --> 00:00:01,950
A test catches ninety percent of

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:04,450
cases, and you test positive.

3
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:05,912
So why is your chance of being

4
00:00:05,912 --> 00:00:07,812
sick only about nine percent?

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,075
Picture a thousand people.

6
00:00:10,075 --> 00:00:11,650
The disease affects one percent of

7
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:13,987
them, so just ten are sick.

8
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,425
The test catches ninety percent of

9
00:00:16,425 --> 00:00:18,700
the sick, so nine of those ten

10
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:19,750
test positive.

11
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,842
But it also flags nine percent of

12
00:00:22,842 --> 00:00:24,092
healthy people.

13
00:00:24,092 --> 00:00:25,280
Nine percent of nine hundred

14
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:27,442
ninety is about eighty-nine more.

15
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:30,121
Your test was positive, so you are

16
00:00:30,121 --> 00:00:31,983
one of these ninety-eight people.

17
00:00:31,983 --> 00:00:33,720
Only nine of them are sick:

18
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:34,921
about nine percent.

19
00:00:35,487 --> 00:00:37,325
In probabilities, the nine is

20
00:00:37,325 --> 00:00:39,925
ninety percent of one percent.

21
00:00:39,925 --> 00:00:42,100
The eighty-nine is nine percent of

22
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:43,825
the other ninety-nine percent.

23
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:45,933
That is Bayes' theorem:

24
00:00:45,933 --> 00:00:47,408
the chance of disease given a

25
00:00:47,408 --> 00:00:49,546
positive is the true positives

26
00:00:49,546 --> 00:00:50,946
over all the positives.

27
00:00:51,567 --> 00:00:54,142
When a disease is rare, false

28
00:00:54,142 --> 00:00:55,504
alarms from the many healthy

29
00:00:55,504 --> 00:00:57,629
people outnumber the real cases

30
00:00:57,629 --> 00:00:58,842
almost ten to one.
